.TH CLOUDIMG-DIFF 1 "November 2026" "cloudimg-diff 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cloudimg-diff \- compare package manifests of Ubuntu cloud image builds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cloudimg-diff serials
.I release
.RB [ \-n
.IR N ]
.br
.B cloudimg-diff diff
.I release
.RI [ old ]
.RI [ new ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cloudimg-diff files
.I old.manifest new.manifest
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cloudimg-diff drift
.I release
.RI [ serial ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B cloudimg-diff compare-versions
.I a op b
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every Ubuntu cloud image published on cloud-images.ubuntu.com has a
.I .manifest
file listing the Debian packages it contains.
.B cloudimg-diff
downloads those manifests and reports which packages were upgraded,
downgraded, added or removed between two builds.
Versions are compared with the same algorithm as
.BR dpkg (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serials
List the most recent release serials of
.I release
(a codename such as
.B noble
or a version such as
.BR 24.04 ).
.TP
.B diff
Compare two published builds.
.I old
and
.I new
are serials (for example
.BR 20261017 )
or the aliases
.BR latest ,
.B previous
and
.BI latest~ N\fR.
The defaults are
.B previous
and
.BR latest .
.TP
.B files
Compare two manifest files on disk.
.TP
.B drift
Compare the packages installed on this machine (as reported by
.BR dpkg-query (1))
with the manifest of the image it was launched from.
.TP
.B compare-versions
Exit with status 0 if the relation
.I a op b
holds, 1 otherwise.
.I op
is one of
.BR "lt le eq ne ge gt << <= = >= >>" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fItable\fR|\fIjson\fR|\fImarkdown\fR
Output format. Markdown output is meant for pull requests and release notes.
.TP
.BI \-\-only " kind"
Show only
.BR added ,
.BR removed ,
.B upgraded
or
.B downgraded
packages. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-exit\-code
Exit with status 1 when there are differences, like
.BR diff (1).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-arch " " \fIarch\fR
Image architecture (default
.BR amd64 ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Always download manifests instead of using the local cache.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/cloudimg-diff/
Downloaded manifests. A published manifest never changes, so cached copies
are kept forever. Inside the snap the cache lives in
.IR $SNAP_USER_COMMON/cache .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when differences were found and
.B \-\-exit\-code
was given (or the relation is false for
.BR compare-versions ),
2 on errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cloudimg-diff diff noble
cloudimg-diff diff noble 20241004 latest \-\-only upgraded \-f markdown
cloudimg-diff drift noble \-\-only added
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg (1),
.BR dpkg-query (1)
